---
title: Bacon, egg and cheese bagels
servings: 6
yield: 6 sandwiches
tags: [pork]
source: Bacon-Egg-Cheese Bagels by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/bacon-egg-cheese-bagel
---

Heat the oven to 350°F. Lay the @bacon{1%lb} on a #baking sheet{} lined with foil and bake until deep golden and crisp. Cool, then dice.

Split the @bagels{6} and toast them in the oven. Thinly slice the @chives{1%bunch}.

Whisk the @eggs{12} with the @half-and-half{1/4%cup} and a pinch of @kosher salt{}.

Melt the @unsalted butter{4%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium heat. Add the eggs and stir gently until about three-quarters set. Fold in the bacon, then the @cheddar{1%cup}(shredded). Take off the heat; the eggs finish cooking on their own.

Pile the eggs onto the bagel bottoms. Spread the tops with the @cream cheese{6%tbsp}, 1 tbsp each.

Finish with @black pepper{}(cracked), @flaked sea salt{} and the chives, and close the sandwiches.

> Heavy cream works in place of the half-and-half.
